{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.reduce_sigma_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.reduce_sigma_squared","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrixOperator.lean#L48-L55","doc":"Reducing `σ·σ` (i.e. `T = σ` acting on `σ`, `a=c=1`, `b=d=0`) recovers the\nHecke relation `σ² = (q − q⁻¹)σ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.reduce_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.reduce_identity","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrixOperator.lean#L40-L46","doc":"The identity operator `T = 0·σ + 1` acts trivially: `(aσ+b) ↦ aσ + b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.reduceB_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.reduceB_def","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrixOperator.lean#L36-L36","doc":"`b' = ca + db` (the constant part). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.reduceA_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.reduceA_def","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrixOperator.lean#L33-L33","doc":"`a' = ca(q − q⁻¹) + cb + da` (the `σ`-part after `σ² = (q−q⁻¹)σ + 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.reduceB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.reduceB","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrixOperator.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Reduced constant `b'` of `(cσ+d)(aσ+b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.reduceA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.reduceA","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrixOperator.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Reduced `σ`-coefficient `a'` of `(cσ+d)(aσ+b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.q","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrixOperator.lean#L27-L27","doc":"Substrate parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrixOperator.lean#L25-L25","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrixOperator","kind":"structure","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TransferMatrixOperator.lean#L20-L36","doc":"Data for the transfer-matrix reduction `(cσ+d)(aσ+b) → a'σ + b'`.\n\nA `definition` carrier: the substrate `q` and the two reduced\ncoordinates `reduceA = a'`, `reduceB = b'` pinned to the Hecke-reduced\ncoefficients of the product. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:transfer-matrix-operator","label":"def:transfer-matrix-operator","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/transfer-matrix-operator.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}